version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arashkermaniprojects/sevim"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
type: software
abstract: >
  SeVim is a five-stage neuro-symbolic pipeline that converts natural-language
  educational text into deterministic, byte-reproducible SVG diagrams without
  hallucination and without external API calls on the default path. It
  combines a rule-based semantic triple extractor, a frozen Qwen2.5-7B
  encoder used solely as a feature extractor, a random-weight linear
  projection to visual parameters seeded at seed=42, and a deterministic
  Sugiyama-style layout engine. A re-runnable cross-system evaluation
  harness ships with the implementation under bench/eval/.
keywords:
  - knowledge graph
  - SVG generation
  - educational technology
  - neuro-symbolic
  - deterministic layout
  - information visualization
